model ul14
  tally 1
  on 2026-10-18
  note "US taxable social security benefits (26 U.S.C. § 86) as IRS Publication 915 (2025) works them: Example 1 (single), Example 3 (the Johnsons, married filing jointly) and the lump-sum election (Terry Jackson, single)."
  note "The worksheet lines are keyed by taxpayer and tax year, so each line reads the law of its year. Worksheet 1 is the regular method for the year. Worksheet 2 is § 86 for the earlier year as if the lump-sum portion attributable to it had been received then (§ 86(e)(1)(A)): the same lines under the pin benefits + lump_for. Worksheet 4 is the year with the earlier years' portions moved out, under the pin benefits − those portions, plus Worksheet 2's line 21 (§ 86(e)(1)(B))."
  note "A line the worksheet leaves blank is '-'. No rounding is stated and every printed line is exact, so no line rounds."
  note "Whether Terry makes the lump-sum election is the taxpayer's choice (§ 86(e)), so it is an axis; the model compares the two methods but never picks one."

source modeller "The model's own readings and assumptions, each stated with its reason"

source pub915 "IRS, Publication 915 (2025), Social Security and Equivalent Railroad Retirement Benefits (Page Last Reviewed or Updated: 30-Apr-2026)" at "https://www.irs.gov/publications/p915"

source publ103_66 "Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1993, Pub. L. 103-66, approved August 10, 1993, § 13215: (a) added § 86(a)(2), the 85 percent tier; (b) amended the heading and text of § 86(c) generally, the base amount and the adjusted base amount; (d) for taxable years beginning after December 31, 1993. The wording is read in 26 U.S. Code § 86 at the Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School, with its Amendments and Effective Date notes" at "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/86"

axis ul14_election
  lump_sum "the taxpayer elects under § 86(e) and reports the Worksheet 4 amount (Form 1040 line 6c checked)"
  regular "the taxpayer doesn't elect and reports the Worksheet 1 amount"

index fstat = [single, hoh, qss, mfs_apart, mfj, mfs_together]

index isrc = [wages, pension, interest, dividends, bond_interest]

index tp = [ex1, johnsons, terry]

index ty = year 2024..2025

input adj[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "What are the adjustments to income (Schedule 1, the worksheet's line 7) for this year?"

input adj_base_amt[s in fstat]: money USD

input base_amt[s in fstat]: money USD

input benefits[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "What net benefits (box 5 of all Forms SSA-1099 and RRB-1099) were received in this year?"

input excl[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "What exclusions does the worksheet's line 5 add back (adoption benefits, foreign earned income or housing, American Samoa or Puerto Rico income)?"

input exempt_int[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "What tax-exempt interest was received or accrued in this year (§ 86(b)(2)(B))?"

input inc[t in tp, y in ty, i in isrc]: money USD question "What income of this kind was there in this year, apart from the benefits?"

input lump_for[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "Which part of the lump-sum benefit payment received in 2025 is attributable to this year?"

input prior_taxable[t in tp, y in ty]: money USD question "What taxable benefits were reported for this earlier year before the lump sum?"

input rate85: num

input status[t in tp, y in ty]: key fstat question "What was the filing status in this year?"

def line6b[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Form 1040 line 6b: the taxable benefits reported under the method chosen."
  rule lump when ul14_election = lump_sum = lump_taxable[t, y]
  rule regular when ul14_election = regular = ws_taxable[t, y]

def ln01[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 1: the benefits of the year. Worksheets 2 and 4 read it under a pin on benefits."
  rule base = benefits[t, y]

def ln02[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 2: one-half of line 1 (§ 86(a)(1)(A), (b)(1)(A)(ii))."
  rule base = ln01[t, y] / 2

def ln03[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 3: the other income of the year. § 86(b)(2) takes modified adjusted gross income without the § 135 exclusion, so excluded savings-bond interest counts (Example 3: '$40,500 ($38,000 + $2,500)')."
  rule base = sum(i in isrc: inc[t, y, i])

def ln04[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD = exempt_int[t, y]

def ln05[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD = excl[t, y]

def ln06[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD = ln02[t, y] + ln03[t, y] + ln04[t, y] + ln05[t, y]

def ln07[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD = adj[t, y]

def ln08[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 8: line 6 less line 7. The worksheet stops before line 8 if line 7 is not less than line 6; that stop is in stop, and line 8 still prints."
  rule base = ln06[t, y] - ln07[t, y]

def ln09[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 9: the base amount for the filing status of the year (§ 86(c)(1)), read at the year's law."
  rule base = base_amt[status[t, y]]

def ln10[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = ln08[t, y] - ln09[t, y]
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln11[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 11: $9,000 or $12,000, the adjusted base amount less the base amount (§ 86(a)(2)(A)(ii), (c)(2))."
  rule base = adj_base_amt[status[t, y]] - base_amt[status[t, y]]
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln12[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = max(0, ln10[t, y] - ln11[t, y])
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln13[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = min(ln10[t, y], ln11[t, y])
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln14[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = ln13[t, y] / 2
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln15[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = min(ln02[t, y], ln14[t, y])
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln16[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = ln12[t, y] * rate85
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln17[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = ln15[t, y] + ln16[t, y]
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln18[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  rule base = ln01[t, y] * rate85
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def ln19[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Line 19: the smaller of line 17 and line 18 (§ 86(a)(2))."
  rule base = min(ln17[t, y], ln18[t, y])
  rule blank excepts base when stop[t, y] = -

def lump_taxable[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Worksheet 4 line 21, the taxable benefits under the election (§ 86(e)(1)): the year's sheet with the lump-sum portions for earlier years moved out of its benefits (lines 1-19, 0 when the sheet stops), plus line 20."
  rule base = ws_taxable[t, y] as if {benefits[t, y] = benefits[t, y] - sum(k in ty where k < y: lump_for[t, k])} + ws4_ln20[t, y]

def over_adj[t in tp, y in ty]: bool
  note "Example 3: more than 50% of the benefits are taxable because line 8 is more than the adjusted base amount."
  rule base = ln08[t, y] > adj_base_amt[status[t, y]]

def smaller[t in tp, y in ty]: bool
  note "Lump-Sum Election, Example: Terry compares Worksheet 4 line 21 with Worksheet 1 line 19."
  rule base = lump_taxable[t, y] < ws_taxable[t, y]

def stop[t in tp, y in ty]: bool
  note "Worksheet lines 7 and 9: none of the benefits are taxable if line 7 is not less than line 6, or if line 8 is not more than line 9 (§ 86(b)(1))."
  rule base = ln07[t, y] >= ln06[t, y] or ln08[t, y] <= ln09[t, y]

def ws2_ln20[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Worksheet 2 line 20: the taxable benefits previously reported for the earlier year; blank when the sheet stops at line 9."
  rule base = prior_taxable[t, y]
  rule blank excepts base when ws2_stop[t, y] = -

def ws2_ln21[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Worksheet 2 line 21: the additional taxable benefits for the earlier year, line 19 refigured with the lump-sum portion for that year (§ 86(e)(1)(A)) less line 20; 0 when the sheet stops at line 9."
  rule base = ln19[t, y] as if {benefits[t, y] = benefits[t, y] + lump_for[t, y]} - ws2_ln20[t, y]
  rule stopped excepts base when ws2_stop[t, y] = 0

def ws2_stop[t in tp, y in ty]: bool
  note "Whether Worksheet 2 stops at line 7 or line 9: the year's stop with the lump-sum portion for that year added to its benefits."
  rule base = stop[t, y] as if {benefits[t, y] = benefits[t, y] + lump_for[t, y]}

def ws4_ln20[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "Worksheet 4 line 20: the total of line 21 of the Worksheets 2 for the earlier years."
  rule base = sum(k in ty where k < y: ws2_ln21[t, k])

def ws_taxable[t in tp, y in ty]: num USD
  note "The sheet's taxable benefits: line 19, or 0 when the sheet stops."
  rule base = ln19[t, y]
  rule stopped excepts base when stop[t, y] = 0

ask q01_ln01: ln01[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q02_ln02: ln02[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q03_ln03: ln03[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q04_ln04: ln04[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q05_ln05: ln05[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q06_ln06: ln06[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q07_ln07: ln07[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q08_ln08: ln08[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q09_ln09: ln09[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q10_ln10: ln10[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q11_ln11: ln11[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q12_ln12: ln12[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q13_ln13: ln13[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q14_ln14: ln14[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q15_ln15: ln15[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q16_ln16: ln16[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q17_ln17: ln17[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q18_ln18: ln18[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q19_ln19: ln19[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q20_ln20: ws2_ln20[terry, 2024], ws4_ln20[terry, 2025]

ask q21_ln21: ws2_ln21[terry, 2024], lump_taxable[terry, 2025]

ask q22_taxable: ws_taxable[t, y] for t in tp, y in [2025]

ask q23_over_adj: over_adj[t, y] for t in [johnsons], y in [2025]

ask q24_smaller: smaller[t, y] for t in [terry], y in [2025]

ask q25_line6b: line6b[t, y] for t in [terry], y in [2025]

ask q26_ws2: ln01[t, y], ln02[t, y], ln03[t, y], ln04[t, y], ln05[t, y], ln06[t, y], ln07[t, y], ln08[t, y], ln09[t, y], ln10[t, y], ln11[t, y], ln12[t, y], ln13[t, y], ln14[t, y], ln15[t, y], ln16[t, y], ln17[t, y], ln18[t, y], ln19[t, y] for t in [terry], y in [2024] with benefits[terry, 2024] = benefits[terry, 2024] + lump_for[terry, 2024]

ask q27_ws4: ln01[t, y], ln02[t, y], ln03[t, y], ln04[t, y], ln05[t, y], ln06[t, y], ln07[t, y], ln08[t, y], ln09[t, y], ln10[t, y], ln11[t, y], ln12[t, y], ln13[t, y], ln14[t, y], ln15[t, y], ln16[t, y], ln17[t, y], ln18[t, y], ln19[t, y] for t in [terry], y in [2025] with benefits[terry, 2025] = benefits[terry, 2025] - lump_for[terry, 2024]

version law_86
  cite publ103_66
  governs 1994..
  known 1993-08-10
  note "Known from the enactment of Pub. L. 103-66, approved August 10, 1993 (Cornell LII, 26 U.S.C. § 86, Amendments: 1993, § 13215(a), (b); Effective Date of 1993 Amendment: § 13215(d), taxable years beginning after December 31, 1993). § 86 itself was added by Pub. L. 98-21, § 121(a), April 20, 1983, but § 13215(b) restated (c) whole, so both amounts of (c) are this act's. The amounts are not indexed; the last amendment of § 86, Pub. L. 117-2 (2021), changed (b)(2)(A) only."
  adj_base_amt = 34000 "§ 86(c)(2)(A): '$34,000'"
  adj_base_amt[mfj] = 44000 "§ 86(c)(2)(B): '$44,000 in the case of a joint return'"
  adj_base_amt[mfs_together] = 0 "§ 86(c)(2)(C): 'zero' for a married taxpayer filing separately who doesn't live apart from the spouse all year"
  base_amt = 25000 "§ 86(c)(1)(A): '$25,000'"
  base_amt[mfj] = 32000 "§ 86(c)(1)(B): '$32,000 in the case of a joint return'"
  base_amt[mfs_together] = 0 "§ 86(c)(1)(C): 'zero'"
  rate85 = 0.85 "§ 86(a)(2)(A)(i) and (B): '85 percent'"

version facts_pub915
  cite pub915
  known 2026-10-18
  note "The examples' stipulations are hypothetical cases: known from the model's on (§4.5), not from the page's update stamp (30-Apr-2026)."
  note "Example 1 and Example 3 are under How Much Is Taxable?; Terry Jackson is under Lump-Sum Election, Example. Lines 4, 5 and 7 are taken from the filled-in worksheets, which print -0- there."
  adj[ex1, 2025] = 0 "Example 1, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 7: -0-"
  adj[johnsons, 2025] = 0 "Example 3, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 7: -0-"
  adj[terry, 2025] = 0 "Terry Jackson's Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 7: -0-"
  benefits[ex1, 2025] = 5980 "Example 1: net benefits of $5,980 in box 5 of Form SSA-1099"
  benefits[johnsons, 2025] = 10000 "Example 3: Jamie's tier 1 railroad benefits, $10,000 in box 5 of Form RRB-1099"
  benefits[terry, 2025] = 11000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example: 'so Terry's total benefits in 2025 were $11,000'"
  excl[ex1, 2025] = 0 "Example 1, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 5: -0-"
  excl[johnsons, 2025] = 0 "Example 3, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 5: -0-"
  excl[terry, 2024] = 0 "Terry Jackson's Filled-in Worksheet 2 line 5: -0-"
  excl[terry, 2025] = 0 "Terry Jackson's Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 5: -0-"
  exempt_int[ex1, 2025] = 0 "Example 1, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 4: -0-"
  exempt_int[johnsons, 2025] = 0 "Example 3, Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 4: -0-"
  exempt_int[terry, 2024] = 0 "Terry Jackson's Filled-in Worksheet 2 line 4: -0-"
  exempt_int[terry, 2025] = 0 "Terry Jackson's Filled-in Worksheet 1 line 4: -0-"
  inc[ex1, 2025] = 0 "Example 1 names a pension, wages and interest only"
  inc[ex1, 2025, wages] = 9400 "Example 1: part-time wages of $9,400"
  inc[ex1, 2025, pension] = 18600 "Example 1: a fully taxable pension of $18,600"
  inc[ex1, 2025, interest] = 990 "Example 1: taxable interest income of $990"
  inc[johnsons, 2025] = 0 "Example 3 names a pension and interest only"
  inc[johnsons, 2025, pension] = 38000 "Example 3: Jessie's fully taxable pension of $38,000"
  inc[johnsons, 2025, interest] = 2300 "Example 3: taxable interest income of $2,300"
  inc[johnsons, 2025, bond_interest] = 200 "Example 3: $200 of qualified U.S. savings bond interest excluded on Form 8815 (in Schedule B line 2)"
  inc[terry, 2024] = 0 "Lump-Sum Election, Example: the 2024 income table lists wages, interest and dividends only"
  inc[terry, 2024, wages] = 20000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2024 income: wages $20,000"
  inc[terry, 2024, interest] = 2000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2024 income: interest income 2,000"
  inc[terry, 2024, dividends] = 1000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2024 income: dividend income 1,000"
  inc[terry, 2025] = 0 "Lump-Sum Election, Example: the 2025 income table lists wages, interest, dividends and a pension only"
  inc[terry, 2025, wages] = 3500 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2025 income: wages $3,500"
  inc[terry, 2025, pension] = 18000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2025 income: fully taxable pension 18,000"
  inc[terry, 2025, interest] = 2500 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2025 income: interest income 2,500"
  inc[terry, 2025, dividends] = 1500 "Lump-Sum Election, Example, 2025 income: dividend income 1,500"
  lump_for[terry, 2024] = 2000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example: a lump sum of $6,000, 'of which $2,000 was for 2024'"
  lump_for[terry, 2025] = 4000 "Lump-Sum Election, Example: '$4,000 was for 2025'"
  status[ex1, 2025] = single "Example 1: you are single and file Form 1040"
  status[johnsons, 2025] = mfj "Example 3: Jamie and Jessie file a joint return"
  status[terry, 2025] = single "Lump-Sum Election, Example: Terry is single"

version model_assume
  cite modeller
  known 2026-10-18
  note "Assumptions standing for the examples' own facts: known from the model's on, as the examples (§4.5)."
  adj[terry, 2024] = 0 assumed "Worksheet 2 line 7 prints -0-; the example states no 2024 adjustments, so 2024 AGI is the income total of $23,000"
  benefits[terry, 2024] = 0 assumed "Worksheet 2 line 1 is $2,000, the lump-sum portion alone, so Terry received no benefits in 2024 itself"
  prior_taxable[terry, 2024] = 0 assumed "Terry had no 2024 benefits before the lump sum, so none were reported as taxable for 2024"
  status[terry, 2024] = single assumed "the 2024 filing status isn't stated; Worksheet 2 line 9 uses $25,000, the single amount"
